        "summary": "cleanup read two answers from stdin unconditionally under set -euo pipefail: with no terminal the first read hit EOF and the script died exit-1 before its own cancel branch, with nothing naming the cause - and cleanup is the only sanctioned removal path, so automated flows had no route. Separately, create resolved its start point to origin/<base> and git's default autoSetupMerge made the new branch track the base's remote branch: safe under push.default=simple, but under upstream a bare git push aimed at the base branch. And the README claimed every skill answers to /flow-next:<name>, which is false for the five phrase-triggered skills two lines before it names them (issue #333 asks a-d).",
        "taskIds": [],
        "title": "The one removal path needed a human at a keyboard"
