        "summary": "cleanup parses its arguments into names plus --yes (any other dash token fails usage; validate_name already rejects leading-dash names so parsing is unambiguous). Names skip the name prompt; the y/N confirmation runs only on a TTY; non-TTY without --yes refuses naming the remedy; non-TTY with no names fails 'no terminal and no names given'; both reads are EOF-guarded. The new-branch create path gains --no-track (existing-branch path untouched). Five regression tests pin the contract tokens, including a no-upstream pin whose fixture asserts the remote-tracking base ref exists so it cannot pass vacuously - mutation-verified to fail without the fix.",
